# Normalize every text file to LF in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# frontend/dist/ is committed but built on BOTH Windows (locally) and Linux
# (CI). Without a fixed EOL the two produce different blobs for the same
# build and CI rewrites dist/ on every push -- 780 lines of pure line-ending
# churn. eol=lf also means Vite reads an LF source index.html on Windows and
# therefore emits an LF dist/index.html, so local and CI builds match byte
# for byte. Every tracked text blob is already LF, so this is a no-op today.
* text=auto eol=lf

# setup.sh / setup-pi.sh are piped into `bash -s` on the Pi (see setup.ps1).
# Covered by the rule above, but called out because the failure mode is ugly:
# a CRLF script hands Linux "$'\r': command not found" on every line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# AD9361 filter configs, generated by the MATLAB Filter Design Wizard in 2015
# and shipped CRLF. They are parsed by pyadi-iio and pushed into the driver,
# so keep the bytes exactly as the vendor produced them.
*.ftr -text

# Vendored/binary assets: never touch.
*.woff2  binary
*.png    binary
*.pkl    binary
*.tar.gz binary
